  "explains": "index in cases/views.py changes (its body). The name is the one every app gives its front page: four modules define a function called index (billing/views.py, billing/reports.py, billing/legacy_views.py and cases/views.py), more than distinct_max = 3, so the name is not distinctive and must not be used to find other code. Which route it serves follows from the imports only: cases/urls.py does `from . import views` and maps path(\"\", views.index), and config/urls.py includes the module object cases_urls under cases/ (a module object, not a string; its app_name, cases, is the namespace). So the route is ANY /cases, from the path() line and the include line. The index view of billing, mounted at /billing, is another function with the same name and is not reached. The web client calls CASES_URL, \"/cases/\", with apiGet; the screen is /cases. The report says not_distinctive for index (not blocking: a stated limit).",
